# GitHub Read-Only Personal Access Token (PAT)
#
# Generate your fine-grained token at:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
#
# Configuration steps:
#   1. Token name: e.g. "agama-bug-maintainer-readonly"
#   2. Expiration: choose desired duration (e.g. 90 days)
#   3. Resource owner / Repository access:
#      - Resource owner: "agama-project" (or your account)
#      - Select "Only select repositories" -> choose "agama-project" repositories (e.g. agama-project/agama)
#   4. Permissions (Strictly Read-Only):
#      - On "Repositories" tab:
#        * Issues: Read-only
#        * Pull requests: Read-only
#        * Metadata: Read-only
#      - On "Organization" tab:
#        * Projects: Read-only
#        (Hint: Projects permissions are on the Organization tab, while the rest are on Repositories tab)
#
# Note: Lines starting with '#' are ignored by run_gemini.sh and run_claude.sh.
# Replace the placeholder below with your real read-only token:
YOUR_GITHUB_READONLY_TOKEN_HERE
